column1:
5:3|I know Ephraim;
Israel is not hidden from me.
Now you have prostituted yourself, Ephraim;
Israel is defiled.|Repeats Ephraim and Israel in both balanced accusations.

9:1|Do not rejoice, Israel;
do not celebrate like the peoples.
You have prostituted yourself, leaving your God;
you have loved a prostitute’s wages
on every grain-threshing floor.|Retains the sexual-economic image at agricultural sites rather than abstracting it into disloyalty.

9:7|The days of reckoning have come;
the days of repayment have come.
Israel will know it.
“The prophet is a fool;
the man of the spirit is mad!”
So great is your guilt, so great your hostility.|Treats the charge as hostile speech while recording the unmarked-speaker alternative in notes.

9:15|“All their evil was at Gilgal;
there I came to hate them.
For the evil of their deeds
I will drive them from my house.
I will love them no longer;
all their rulers are rebels.|Keeps the hard divine declarations and rulers/rebels wordplay in a clear close.
